# CPU frequency governor selection.
#
# NOT STOCK -- this whole file is ours. Nothing equivalent ships in
# ADVAN_6781_S34NF2_V4.0_20250304.
#
# The kernel this device ships with (device/advan/6781-kernel) provides the
# `reflex` governor (itel-rs4-kernel vanilla: config/reflex.fragment +
# apply-reflex.sh, all variants). Select it explicitly on both policies.
#
# THE TRIGGER MATTERS. Stock init.cgroup.rc -- which this tree ships and
# stock's init.mt6789.rc imports -- writes `sugov_ext` to these same two
# nodes in post-fs-data (measured in the stock file). Actions bound to one
# trigger run in the order init parsed them, which depends on import order,
# so competing writes in post-fs-data would be decided by something as
# fragile as a line's position in an import list. `on boot` fires strictly
# after `on post-fs-data`, so this write wins regardless. (sugov_ext IS
# present in a GKI kernel -- scaling_available_governors lists it -- so
# init.cgroup.rc's write really does take effect; keep that file for its
# uclamp and boot-perf tuning.)
#
# On a kernel without `reflex` the write below fails the way any bad
# scaling_governor write does -- non-fatal, and the policy keeps whatever
# it had (sugov_ext from init.cgroup.rc, or the kernel default). That is
# deliberate: this file must not break a build that swaps the kernel out.
#
# policy0 = 6x Cortex-A55 (little), policy6 = 2x Cortex-A76 (big). Topology
# from the stock dtb (cpu@000-005 + cpu@100-101, the only 8 cpu nodes).
# Tester gate before release: related_cpus of policy0 reads "0 1 2 3 4 5"
# and policy6 reads "6 7", and scaling_governor reads reflex on both.

on boot
    write /sys/devices/system/cpu/cpufreq/policy0/scaling_governor reflex
    write /sys/devices/system/cpu/cpufreq/policy6/scaling_governor reflex

    chown system system /sys/devices/system/cpu/cpufreq/policy0/scaling_governor
    chown system system /sys/devices/system/cpu/cpufreq/policy6/scaling_governor
    chmod 0660 /sys/devices/system/cpu/cpufreq/policy0/scaling_governor
    chmod 0660 /sys/devices/system/cpu/cpufreq/policy6/scaling_governor
